{{!
    @template local_learningjourney/partial_progress

    Accessible course progress bar and its supporting text.

    The visual fill is driven by a CSS custom property so the bar can animate
    without any JavaScript, and is hidden from assistive technology because the
    progressbar element already carries the value.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * percent int Whole number percentage of course completion.
    * percentlabel string Readable form of the percentage.
    * unitlabel string Description of the current unit, such as Lesson 1 of 5.
    * hasunitlabel bool Whether the unit label is known.
    * progressline string Sentence describing remaining work.
    * hasline bool Whether the supporting sentence is present.
    * arialabel string Accessible name of the progress bar.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "percent": 20,
        "percentlabel": "20% complete",
        "unitlabel": "Lesson 1 of 5",
        "hasunitlabel": true,
        "progressline": "Only 4 lessons remaining.",
        "hasline": true,
        "arialabel": "Course completion"
    }
}}
<div class="ljy-progress">
    {{#hasunitlabel}}<p class="ljy-progress__unit">{{unitlabel}}</p>{{/hasunitlabel}}
    <div class="ljy-progress__track"
         role="progressbar"
         aria-label="{{arialabel}}"
         aria-valuenow="{{percent}}"
         aria-valuemin="0"
         aria-valuemax="100"
         aria-valuetext="{{percentlabel}}"
         style="--ljy-progress-value: {{percent}}%;">
        <span class="ljy-progress__fill" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
    <p class="ljy-progress__percent" aria-hidden="true">{{percentlabel}}</p>
    {{#hasline}}<p class="ljy-progress__text">{{progressline}}</p>{{/hasline}}
</div>
